    {
      "id": "recap",
      "chapter": "Recap",
      "narration": "A cookie is a small piece of text a site stores in your browser. It lets the site recognize you, keep you logged in, and remember your cart. It can also let advertisers track you across sites. This week, open your browser settings and look at the cookies saved there. Delete the ones you don't recognize.",
